  "worked_solution": "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =169 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(169) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (2x)+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (2y) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, substituting the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=5$ and $y=12,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (2x)+5\\cdot (2(12)) & =0 \\\\ 2x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+120 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also want to substitute for $x,$ but we are not given this value. However, we can find it by substituting $y=12$ into the equation of the circle.  \n\nAt the point where $y=12,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =169 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{12}^{2} & =169 \\\\ {x}^{2}+144 & =169 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =25 \\\\ x & =\\pm 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe choose $x=5$ since we're only interested in the first quadrant. \n\nFinally, substituting $x=5,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+120 & =0 \\\\ 2(5)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+120 & =0 \\\\ 10\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-120 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{-120}{10} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
